Change: Expected WebDAV client errors are no longer logged as fatal

Every WebDAV error that the exception logger did not know as expected went into
owncloud.log at level fatal. That included requests the desktop client sends
as part of its normal work: MKCOL on a folder that already exists answers
"405 The resource you tried to create already exists", and a test instance
collected more than 500 of these fatal entries in two days of sync tests, which
buried the few entries that mattered.

The following client errors are now logged at debug level, like the ones that
were already treated as expected (404, 412, 423 and others): 405 Method Not
Allowed, 409 Conflict (also when a lock token does not match), 411 Length
Required, 415 for an unsupported REPORT, 416 Requested Range Not Satisfiable
and 501 Not Implemented.

400 Bad Request, other 415 errors and 503 stay at level fatal, because they can
point to a problem on the server side, for example an upload whose size does not
match or content that a storage rejected.
